    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376-a1">

                <pb facs="0699" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg637"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 805.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bowen to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The Manufacturers’ Association of the Northwest</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Chicago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-08-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 23, 1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Please find herein cards of invitation
                    to the reception tendered his excellency, the Mexican minister, by the
                    Manufacturers of the Northwest, and we should be pleased to see you, but
                    distance no doubt will prevent.</p>
                <p>We feel disposed to do some business with the citizens of the Republic of Mexico,
                    as Chicago produces many articles it seems to me consumed there, and I shall be
                    pleased to have any views you may have gained, during your residence in the city
                    of Mexico, on that subject.</p>
                <p>I am, dear sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. S. BOWEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
